  "conditions": {
    "dedicated": true,
    "detail": "Box dedicated to this run, and that is the point for this engine: the bring-up's bf16 attempt was killed by the memory watchdog with the recipe server holding 65 GB, leaving it about 41 GB. Here nothing else was resident -- every other engine in this campaign was stopped and confirmed gone first. Ambient temperature unknown (no sensor on this box).",
    "isolation_check": "nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps was empty before the server started and listed only the vLLM worker while it ran; pgrep found no other engine. A 1 Hz sampler recorded the sum of --query-compute-apps and free -m for the whole run, and a second 1 Hz guard watched free -m during the load with a 112000 MiB abort."
  },
  "gotchas": [
    {
      "severity": "blocker",
      "text": "This lane has no transparency parameter, so the images were rendered without one: what was measured is the API, not the model's RGBA mode."
    },
    {
      "severity": "warn",
      "text": "The driver reported thermal/hardware slowdown during the run — the numbers are throttled."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "nvidia-smi --query-gpu=memory.used returns [N/A] on GB10: the CPU and the GPU share one pool and the per-device counter is not implemented. vram_peak_gb here comes from the sum of --query-compute-apps=used_memory, which the harness falls back to."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "--gpu-memory-utilization does not bound this path. It is accepted and echoed back in the server's non-default args, and then has no effect: it sizes the autoregressive KV cache, while the diffusion stage loads every component resident regardless. There is no equivalent of SGLang's auto memory policy here -- short of memory this engine keeps allocating rather than downgrading to offload, which is how the bring-up's bf16 attempt died. It is therefore not passed in this run; the box was made empty instead."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "--diffusion-quantization-config's help text shows only the flat form {\"method\":\"fp8\",\"activation_scheme\":\"dynamic\"}. The per-component dict this model's own recipe uses is undocumented there, but quantization/factory.py detects it (no top-level method key) and the server confirms it in the log with 'Per-component quantization'. ignored_layers img_mlp is the vendor's own recommendation for this model and is what the FP8 configuration here passes."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Seed semantics are per engine and this one differs from the reference lane's. At seed 42 vLLM-Omni produces a different, equally valid scene from the diffusers pipeline that made the bf16 bundle, so eval-t2i-fidelity-v1 on this lane is a scene-match number and NOT a quality number. Read the perceptual-hash Hamming distance rather than the PSNR to tell the two apart: quantization noise keeps it near zero, a different noise draw does not."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "enforce_eager defaults to false, so CUDA graphs are captured on the first request and that capture sits inside the first measured render unless it is warmed. The harness renders warmup_requests first and excludes them, so the published percentiles are warm; the bring-up measured the cold/warm gap at 4.8 percent."
    }
  ],
